{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "c0d49566-8fa9-814e-b34b-9651df48f663",
  "created_at": "2026-01-27T13:07:30-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Donna Iannuccilli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:00:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:00:42-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, good afternoon. Can you hear me okay? I'm on my cell and it's not great in the house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:00:51-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you. A little scratchy but go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:00:56-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. My name is Donna Iannuccilli. I'm calling because the plow came down my street and buried my car. Plowed me right in. I've got a wall of that heavy stuff behind and in front of the car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:13-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's no fun. Which street are you on, Donna?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Twenty-six Mill Street. Up on the Hill. [line breaks up] ...the car is parked right out front, on the street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:27-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up on me there. Twenty-six Mill Street, you said?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:33-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, twenty-six Mill. Twenty-six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:36-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And when did this happen? Was it during the storm?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:01:42-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it was that snow-to-rain thing, Sunday into Monday. It started snow, then turned to rain, and now what's left is like cement. The plow went by yesterday I think, early, and left this big ridge. I went out this morning to move the car and I'm not going anywhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:02:04-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that wet stuff gets heavy fast. Is the car blocking anything, or is it just stuck in place?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:02:13-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just stuck. I shoveled a little and my back said no thank you. I'm seventy-some years old, I'm not chipping through that. So I'm wondering when somebody's coming to clear it. [crosstalk]"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:02:27-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, go ahead, I talked over you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:02:31-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, you go. I just said, when is somebody coming to clear it out?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:02:38-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So here's the thing. The plows push snow to the side of the road, and that's going to bank up against parked cars. The crews don't usually come back to dig out individual cars. I can log the complaint with the location, and if the street needs another pass, they'll see that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:01-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So nobody's coming to dig me out. That's what you're telling me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:07-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not specifically to dig out the car, no. I don't want to tell you something that isn't true. But I can put in a note for your block so the supervisor knows it's heavy there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:23-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. Well. Put the note in. I'll be honest, it's a little aggravating. I moved the car off the road the night before like you're supposed to, or I tried, and there's no room on Mill Street. Everybody's on the street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:41-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. The Hill is tight with the narrow streets. Is there any driveway or lot nearby where you could put it once it's out?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:53-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, not really. [line breaks up] ...neighbor's got a spot but he's away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:03:59-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I lost you again. You said a neighbor?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, never mind, it's not important. Just the car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:08-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Let me get this down. Twenty-six Mill Street, car parked on the street, plowed in from Monday's pass. Is it a call-back number you want to leave?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:21-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's 401-555-0199."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:23-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-nine. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:26-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:28-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Now, in the meantime, with the rain turning it to slush and then freezing, it's going to be rough. If you have a neighbor or someone who could help with a shovel, that's honestly going to be quicker than waiting."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:04:46-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I know, I know. I'll find somebody. There's a kid down the street who does it for a few bucks. I just hate paying for something when the city's the one who buried me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:05:01-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. I'll make sure the note is in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:05:06-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And you know what, while I'm on, this is going to sound silly. I was cleaning out the junk drawer in the kitchen this morning, waiting for the snow to melt, and I found an old key. Little brass thing. I have no idea what it opens. Is there any chance it's something the city would know about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:05:32-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A key? Hm. Not that I'd know. Is there a tag or a number stamped on it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:05:40-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a number on it, but it's all worn. Nothing else. It's not a house key, I tried the doors. Not the cellar either, I went down cellar and tried the padlock on the old coal bin, nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:05:57-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's probably a padlock or a cabinet or a mailbox from years ago. The city wouldn't have a record of it from this department. If it's an old building key, you might ask whoever owned the house before."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:06:14-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Probably. I'll keep trying around the house. Up attic maybe. There's an old trunk up there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:06:22-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a good bet. Trunks always have those little keys."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:06:27-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. Okay, so back to my car. You said the note goes to the supervisor. Is there a way I could find out if somebody comes?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:06:39-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't promise a visit. But if you call back tomorrow morning and give the address, whoever picks up can tell you if anything was scheduled for your street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:06:52-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So tomorrow I call back. Fine. It's just, you'd think after they plow you in, they'd come back and deal with it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:07:03-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I know it feels that way. It's a common complaint after a storm like this, and I'm sorry. I really am."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:07:13-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thank you for putting it in, Denise. That's your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:07:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, Denise. You take care out there, and be careful with that shovel."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:07:25-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I will. Bye now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T13:07:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bye bye."
    }
  ],
